{
    "name": "target-per-period-a-modifier-replaces-the-target-and-a-vacation-week-is-any-overlap",
    "why": "Two decisions in one world, because they are only ever exercised together. Owner decision M makes a matching modifier REPLACE the level's own number rather than adjust it — adding the modifier's 2 to the base 4 gives 6 and flags p-ali, ignoring modifiers altogether gives 4 and flags them too, and only replacement leaves them clean. Owner decision N carries AvailabilitySummary's vacation-week rule VERBATIM: any overlap with a week's clipped bounds is a whole vacation week, so p-ali's Thursday-to-Monday leave is TWO weeks and p-noor's Sunday-to-Thursday leave is ONE, though p-noor's is the longer of the two by a day. Counting only weeks the leave covers whole gives p-ali nought and flags them. The engine and the rota screen reporting different counts for the same person in the same period is a disagreement nobody could adjudicate from either screen, which is why the rule is carried rather than rewritten.",
